{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they both dreamed a dream.</b> וַיַּחְלְמוּ שְׁנֵיהֶם חֲלוֹם — this is its plain sense; and its midrash: each one dreamed both dreams — that he dreamed his own dream and the interpretation of his fellow's, and this is what is said: ״וַיַּרְא שַׂר הָאֹפִים כִּי טוֹב פָּתַר.״" "<b>Each man according to the interpretation of his dream.</b> Each one dreamed a dream resembling the interpretation that was destined to come upon them."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:47.271337120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}